## Nominal 30 mL / 20% finish, only after execution clearance

Use a measured 6.00 mL homogeneous concentrate aliquot at a recorded temperature, recording its actual mass m6_g. Bring to final 30.00 mL with suitable perfumer's ethanol in calibrated final-volume equipment. Do not blindly add 24 mL or call 6 g equal to 6 mL.

For any row, actual product mass in bottle = m6_g * master_product_mg / 6000.
Record final bottle mass M_g. Finished ppm w/w = actual_product_g / M_g * 1,000,000.
Individual raw-stock µL and literal active µL remain UNKNOWN until the appropriate physical measurements exist.

Record: date; preparer; bottle IDs; preparation IDs; actual addition masses; total; temperature; concentrate aliquot volume and mass; ethanol used; final volume and mass; clarity/precipitation; departures. Do not compensate a mistake by silently changing a later ingredient.

Current computational decision: pipeline FAIL / controlling release HOLD. This card confers no physical compounding, skin testing, safety, stability, sensory similarity or release authority.

